-- title:
--   An arbitrary seed replacement preserves the prebridge ledger
-- statement:
--   Fix a structured bridge on head-simplex tags, bank realization, and guarded anchor certificate. Let old and new seeds be supported through the structured active values in the complete guarded smooth row. Assume the outside selector agrees with the old ambient seed on active values outside the broad correction pool. Suppose the new minus old active mass is an integer $d$, and their valuation moments agree at every prime $q\le W$. For the additive placement based on the old two-zero-cell source selector,
--
--   $$\sum_{a\in\mathrm{smooth\ row}}(s_{\rm new}(a)-s_{\rm base}(a))=d,\qquad\sum_{a\in\mathrm{smooth\ row}}(s_{\rm new}(a)-s_{\rm base}(a))v_q(a)=0\quad(q\le W\text{ prime}).$$
--
--   These are precisely the support, integral mass, and head-moment fields of the prebridge moment ledger.
